---
/**
 * "A closer look" — cómo trabajo, y qué lo gobierna.
 *
 * ⚠️ Esta página es la PRÁCTICA, en primera persona. La metodología como
 * artefacto generalizable tiene su propia ficha de proyecto: aquí se enlaza y
 * no se describe. El reparto es lo que evita que esta página envejezca cada
 * vez que se mueve la constitución — lo que versiona es la ficha; una práctica
 * cambia mucho más despacio.
 *
 * ⚠️ AX-9: techo de 800 palabras visibles. La versión anterior tenía 2.187 y
 * se leía en once minutos, contra un objetivo declarado de que un PI entienda
 * en uno. Lo que se corta no se pierde: es lo que deja hueco a que pregunten,
 * que es para lo que existe el sitio.
 *
 * Forma: presentación · overview · puerta. Las figuras se DIBUJAN desde los
 * tokens (AX-8); las dos fotografías que quedaban se retiran con el recorte
 * salvo el grafo, que no se puede redibujar.
 */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SessionLoop from "../../components/SessionLoop.astro";
import ClauseGrid from "../../components/ClauseGrid.astro";
import GovernanceLoop from "../../components/GovernanceLoop.astro";
import PermissionTable from "../../components/PermissionTable.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../utils/url";
import { LINKS } from "../../consts";
---

<Base
  title="A closer look — how I work"
  description="How I run research with AI agents doing the execution: one active front, a plan that records reasoning as it happens, and write rules that decide what a machine may put in the record."
>
  <article class="closer">
    <div class="container closer__wrap">
      <a class="closer__back" href={withBase("/#how-title")}>← Back to how I work</a>

      <header class="closer__header">
        <span class="mono-label">How I work · a closer look</span>
        <h1>A research record that AI can write into</h1>
        <p class="closer__lede">
          Three things slowed me down: I couldn't hold everything I'd studied,
          I lost time to planning itself, and then AI agents started writing
          files inside my projects that I'd have to trust months later. This is
          what I run daily, across a thesis, a lab platform and this site.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="closer__walk">
        <!-- 1 · La práctica, en movimiento -->
        <section class="closer__phase">
          <h2 class="closer__phase-title">What a working session looks like</h2>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            One front is active at a time; everything else waits in order,
            saying what it waits on. A list of eight parallel priorities never
            contradicts reality, so it never gets corrected.
          </p>
          <SessionLoop />
        </section>

        <!-- 2 · Lo que lo gobierna -->
        <section class="closer__phase">
          <h2 class="closer__phase-title">What governs it</h2>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            When two rules collide, the clause they serve breaks the tie. It is
            slower than not doing it, and that's the trade, stated as one:
            productivity spent to buy traceability and understanding.
          </p>
          <ClauseGrid />
        </section>

        <!-- 3 · El centro de gravedad: quién puede escribir el registro -->
        <section class="closer__phase">
          <h2 class="closer__phase-title">Rules for machines that write</h2>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            Agents don't just answer — they execute, and they write into the
            record I rely on. An agent that tidies a decision log has destroyed
            the evidence that log existed to hold, and nothing in the diff looks
            alarming.
          </p>

          <GovernanceLoop />

          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            The agent is the sole author of code. What it may never be is the{" "}
            <em>originator</em> of a change to the record: what it concludes on
            its own goes to a mailbox, signed, and I integrate it or I don't.
          </p>

          <PermissionTable />

          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            The other half is an obligation to refuse. Whoever plans is reading
            a conversation; whoever executes is reading the repository, and only
            one of them sees the real state. Executing an instruction you can
            demonstrate is wrong is the failure. Refusing isn't.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 4 · Dónde se rompe: el número, y por qué existe la interfaz -->
        <section class="closer__phase">
          <h2 class="closer__phase-title">Where it breaks, and what I'm building next</h2>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            It names the volume it was built for — ten projects, fifty open
            items — and which step goes manual first. A design that hasn't
            stated its breaking point was designed for today.
          </p>
          <p class="closer__phase-intro">
            It also pays a cost I chose: everything live sits in one central
            set, because you never choose work one project at a time. One long
            file is harder to read than eleven short ones — <em>until something
            filters it</em>. I'm building that filter: a visual environment over
            the live set, for me and for anyone with more projects than a list
            can hold.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- 5 · La puerta -->
      <section class="closer__doors" aria-labelledby="doors-title">
        <h2 id="doors-title" class="closer__phase-title">Three ways to go deeper</h2>
        <ul class="closer__door-list">
          <li>
            <a href={withBase("/work/mlabs")}>The methodology as its own project</a>
            <span>Public and versioned — split off so that whether it generalises is testable rather than flattering.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href={withBase("/work/tfm/process")}>The thesis, decision by decision</a>
            <span>Thirteen design calls, each with the alternative it turned down and what choosing cost.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>Ask me about any of it</a>
            <span>Deliberately short. What's worth asking is what got cut, and which rules turned out to be theatre.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .closer {
    padding-block: var(--space-xl) var(--space-2xl);
  }
  .closer__wrap {
    max-width: 54rem;
  }
  .closer__back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .closer__header {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    border-bottom: var(--border);
  }
  .closer__header h1 {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
  }
  .closer__lede {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .closer__walk {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
  }
  /* Los grid items traen min-width:auto y no encogen por debajo de su
     contenido: en móvil eso empujaba las figuras y la tabla más allá del
     viewport y hacía scrollear la página entera en horizontal. */
  .closer__walk > * {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .closer__phase-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 30%, transparent);
  }
  .closer__phase-intro {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }
  /* Un párrafo que precede a una figura va más pegado a ella: la figura es
     su continuación, no un bloque aparte. Y el que la sigue necesita aire,
     o el pie de figura y el párrafo se leen como el mismo bloque. */
  .closer__phase-intro + :global(figure) {
    margin-top: calc(var(--space-lg) * -1 + var(--space-md));
  }
  :global(figure) + .closer__phase-intro {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  /* La puerta. Va fuera del recorrido y con su propio ritmo: es lo único de
     la página que pide una acción. */
  .closer__doors {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: var(--border);
  }
  .closer__door-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .closer__door-list {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }
  .closer__door-list li {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    max-width: none;
    align-content: start;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    border: var(--border);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--paper);
    transition: border-color var(--dur) var(--ease),
      box-shadow var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }
  .closer__door-list li:hover {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 45%, var(--line));
    border-top-color: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.05);
  }
  .closer__door-list a {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .closer__door-list span {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }
</style>
